WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Securities. Please go ahead.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:08.860
Oh, thank you so much. Some of your competitors are becoming increasingly vocal about extending

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.400
big LOEs at the end of the decade.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.860
Novartis is the notable exception. It could be attributed to nothing more than communication

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:24.080
practices. But if Novartis feels it has a good shot at delaying Cosentix LOE, then why not note

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.560
that? And if this is an area of active pursuit, what is it that you're doing? Co-formulation,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:35.900
extended dosing. And related to all this, if Karen Hale is in the room, can she compare and

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.920
contrast this to her experience at AbbVie? Thank you.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.340
Yeah, thanks.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.340
Thanks, Steve. So, you know, Karen Hale is in the room, but I'll spare her from having to compare

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:52.540
her thoughts with AbbVie. I think that would be not the appropriate setting to do that. But we

00:00:52.540 --> 00:01:00.460
appreciate the question. I mean, of course, we have extensive efforts to defend our IP and then

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.640
look at other ways to, you know, formulate our medicines. I mean, a good example is the Cosimta

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.920
two-month, which we do have now, planned readout. We have additional efforts as well to life cycle

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.260
manage.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.840
We have additional efforts to do the Cosimta into longer intervals as well, which are still in the,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.180
you know, early phases of efforts. We'll see how that progresses. All of that would generate

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:28.280
new IP, I think. And so that one is clear. I think with Cosentix, we have a number of cell

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.340
line formulation and other patents that we continue to prosecute. We, as a practice, don't

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:40.920
add those in as potential scenarios until we've gotten further along, I think, in the litigation

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.880
phase to really understand where, you know, where those trials ultimately fit. So I think with

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.940
Cosentix, with Cosimta, many efforts. I think we've discussed extensively with Cascali the efforts

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:59.340
around CDK2, CDK2-4, the picovation efforts as well. Harder with a small molecule, as you know,

